<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19445" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gĕnĭcŭlum</span></b> ,
			i, n.
		dim.
		genu, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a little knee</i>, <i>a knee.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b> (ante- and postclass.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pueris in geniculis alligare serperastra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 9, § 11</span></i>
			 Müll.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">de geniculis adorare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Cor. Mil. 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dissolutio geniculorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Nah. 2, 10</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a knot</i> or <i>joint</i> on the stalk of a plant, <i><span class="en">Plin. 26,
				11, 71, § 117</span></i>; <i><span class="en">18, 7, 10, §
			56</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
